)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: Printer Panel -- Fields                  !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                   }
}
{  PRINTER  }The printer's name.
{  STATUS   }Its state as JES2 gives it: INACTIVE, ACTIVE, DRAINED, ...
{  SFORM    }The forms it prints. Can be overtyped: $T with F=.
{  SCLASS   }The output classes it prints. Can be overtyped: $T with Q=.
{  JOBNAME, TYPE, JNUM }The job an active printer is printing.
}
}  PF11 shows the fields further right, PF10 goes back. Of those, SDSF
}  fills SFCB (the FCB image; overtype it: $T with C=), SUCS (the print
}  train), SEP (separator pages; YES or NO: $T with S=) and SDEST1 (the
}  route; LOCAL or Un: $T with R=), and shows the JES2 defaults for
}  WORK-SELECTION, SBURST, SPRMODE1, CKPTLINE and CKPTPAGE. The other
}  fields are not filled yet.
}
}  Overtyping needs UPDATE access to SDSF.OPER; the panel says COMMAND
}  ISSUED, Enter shows the new value. SFORM and SCLASS share one field.
}
}
}
}
}
}  Enter: next topic   PF7: Printer panel help   PF3: back to SDSF
